A||||23||JBGehling||Wrecked!||||8||
Z||000000||JBGehling||12-31-2000||06:44 PM||||Today was a really cruddy day.<BR> I got in a wreck that absolutely wasn't my fault. Someone pulled directly in front of me with about 15 ft. between us and me doing around 50 MPH! And it was a damned mustang, no less! <BR>My TOTALLY stock 88 GT with near PERFECT original paint, has a wrecked front end. Of course, it's going to be paid for, but nothing can fix how bad I feel about wrecking this beautiful car (even though it wasn't my fault). Oh well, just had to share this with someone. The whole hood, front fenders, windshield and door will have to be replaced.<P>Of course, the person I ran into didn't seem to give a ****  about what happened to her car and I was nearly in tears...<P>Anyways, Happy New Year, I hope yours is going better than mine. <P>Josh<P>------------------<BR>88 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/small.gif"> <BR>In Search of: 85 GT, 86 SE or 87 SE (must be manual transmission and low miles)||||reg||8
Z||000001||2xsess||12-31-2000||06:51 PM||||Oh man, That sucks big time. I can't imagine how that must feel as I've never owned such a beautiful example of factory paint.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||12-31-2000||07:24 PM||||OMG!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! I'm so sorry!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> If it was me, i would get a life long perscription for prozac! Sorry man! Are you going to have it fixed or is it totaled?<BR>Alex... <P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||07:30 PM||||MAN.........that really sucks!! I always stay at home during holidays just because theres so many friggin idiots on the road. (or I drive 'Battlestar Galactica' an 88 Lincoln Town Car, no one ever pulls out in front of it, darn it, I could use the insurance money.)||||reg||1
Z||000004||JBGehling||12-31-2000||07:51 PM||||It's definitely not totalled, but it's going to need alot of work. My dad suggested a totally new paint job instead of just the front. I'm going to get to drive a 1991 Signature Series Lincoln Town Car until it gets fixed, which could be a couple months  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> if we do the repaint.<BR>Here's what I was thinking, now that the car's not stock (hurts to say it!): Repaint it yellow with some nice chrome five-spoke wheels. Take off the rear spoiler. Add T-tops. Black Leather interior. And maybe get the headlight kit that has clear headlight covers (I.E. 300ZX) that don't pop up. Does Anyone know where to get this kit?<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000005||AkursedX||12-31-2000||08:52 PM||||Man, I'm really sorry to hear that.  I own the exact same type of Fiero, same color and everything but minus the spoiler.  And I know I would be destroyed if my baby got wrecked.  <BR>Just be glad that'll be getting paid for.  ||||reg||9
Z||000006||rodmcneill||12-31-2000||08:58 PM||||Sorry to hear about the accident. Hopefully you will really like whatever you create next.||||reg||9
Z||000007||JBGehling||12-31-2000||09:03 PM||||        ok, now this is getting heated. A police officer just called the house and said that the other party had found an eyewitness. This eyewitness, who just happens to be the girl's aunt, says that the girl was "just pulling out to see what was coming" and that I came out of nowhere and just (I guess) decided to ram the girl in the side. Now, no matter how ludicrous this sounds (and the fact that the officer investigated and said that it was blatantly her fault), the officer has decided to now change the ticket to be totally my fault! That's right, because of one eyewitness, the whole situation has to be paid for by me. <BR>This just keeps getting better and better. I absolutely cannot believe this is happening. I am in total shock. How can an eyewitness change an investigation of the scene? *I hit the girl's car in the VERY back. And the tire of my car that hit the other car was sitting on the white line, that means the whole car was ahead of it! This is stupid!<BR>Unbelievable!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex2004||12-31-2000||09:10 PM||||You can get some really awesome (non-pop up)headlight kit at  <A HREF="http://www.gscustom.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gscustom.com</A>  They have the clear cover and look awesome. <BR>here is a pic of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.gscustom.com/headlight_right.jpg">  <P>Alex<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex2004||12-31-2000||09:13 PM||||OMG, that is so freaking stupid. That doesn't seem right, that they can just change it!!! Umm, it was her damn aunt, she probably wasn't even an eyewitness! UGH, that's so stupid...Sorry man!<BR>Alex||||reg||8
Z||000010||GeeDee86GT||12-31-2000||09:33 PM||||Tough luck, Josh.  I know some of the forum members are police officers so I hope you'll get some good advice.  In Canada this is a trip to court to fight it. Try to get as much documentation as possible.  Take photos of the spot showing where the cars were, etc.  The officer will have notes from the initial investigation which may be favourable to you. get all the witnesses (real ones?) to make a note for you if there were any.  Good luck.<BR>Gary||||reg||8
Z||000011||Hank is Here||12-31-2000||09:34 PM||||I feel your pain about the car. Had an  accident happened to me three months ago or so.  Mess up my car with about 128xxx on it. Needless to pay I was miffed but oh well.  got the front facia painted on someone elses nickle and looks new.  128,xxx of stone and road drbris took its tole on the paint though it still looked okay.  <P>I would have a long talk with the cop about whose fault it is.  <P>Mark Johnson ||||reg||1
Z||000012||zeusrekning||12-31-2000||09:57 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Man i'm sorry, Get your cousin or something to say he was walking down the road and seen the whole thing <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000013||fiero56||12-31-2000||10:01 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Black88GT||12-31-2000||11:09 PM||||Same thing happened to me, some old lady ran a stop sign and turned into my lane, yet since I was going about 45 in a 35, and she had a witness who happened to be her niece, she got off scott free and I was left with a damaged yellow formula.  <P>Welcome to the BS world of insurance company's.  If you haven't realized by now, they have the politicians in their pockets, so any new insurance law will NOT be in your favor.  The law I got screwed under was called "contributory negligence", basically so the insurance company can get out of paying people who have paid them all their lives.  Being a young male further lessens your case...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||6
Z||000015||JBGehling||12-31-2000||11:20 PM||||ok, I've got what the eyewitness said and apparently, what convinced the officer it was totally my fault. After I had gotten out of the car and finished with a string of cuss words. Another person who was sitting behind the girl who pulled in front of me asked me if I was ok, and I mustered up the words to say yes. Then the woman went over to the girl and they talked for a long time and then she asked the girl if she wanted her to stay to be a witness and the girl said no (I believe this was the aunt). I walked over to the woman, because, for all intents and purposes, it should've been me she was comforting  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (because the girl blatantly pulled out in front of me and more damage was done to my car) so I said "you don't think this is my fault?!" to the witness and she told me that "I'm sorry but it was" (apparently she took it like I said it was my fault, I guess). <BR>So I guess the girl had gotten the witness' number, gave it to the officer, and he called when we left. At least my mom took some pictures of the scene. <BR>So a witness can rule out every bit of evidence at the place of the wreck?<BR>Weird thing is: I still haven't received a ticket for what happened today.<BR>||||reg||1
